      "problem": "Express $\\sqrt[3]{5} \\approx 1.709$ in an equivalent logarithmic form.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the given approximation can be written using exponents:\n\n$$\n5^{1/3} \\approx 1.709\n$$\n\nThe logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a = b^x$ is equivalent to $\\log_{b}{a} = x$\n\nIf we compare $5^{1/3} \\approx 1.709$ with $a = b^x,$ we get $a = 1.709, b = 5,$ and $x=\\dfrac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the approximation $\\sqrt[3]{5} \\approx 1.709$ is equivalent to $\\log_{5}(1.709) \\approx \\dfrac{1}{3}.$",
